{
  "format": 2,
  "id": "capacity-and-draw-share",
  "rev": 1,
  "name": "Machines offer their input's capacity and pay only for their share; Conversion Loss costs power",
  "description": "Written against upstream 459e423 (TrueGrid 1.3.5). Supersedes converter-draw-share rev 1. Three changes to Build_TrueGridMachine_Base EventGraph: (U) Upstream Production Capacity reads the input circuit's GetPowerProductionCapacity again (1.3.4 behaviour) instead of its last produced point, so chains fed by fuel generators are no longer capped at the generators' current output; (C1/C3) each machine's input draw is its share of each output circuit's consumption (consumed x clamp(own base production / circuit produced, 0, 1)) in the main loop and the inductor Smoothing Timer; (C2) Conversion Loss multiplies the draw by (2 - Conversion % Penalty). All three touch the same asset, so they ship as one patch.",
